Uganda's health minister on Tuesday declared the country Ebola-free, following the latest outbreak of the viral haemorrhagic disease which infected 20 people and killed two in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f4cd4230-638d-11f1-9da1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-08T152058Z-1723229578-RC2IPLAHRTG4-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-UGANDA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f4cd4230-638d-11f1-9da1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-08T152058Z-1723229578-RC2IPLAHRTG4-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-UGANDA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84d0caee-8a87-11f1-bfd4-3d2e56de2bfc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 29 Jul 2026 09:39:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f4cd4230-638d-11f1-9da1-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-08T152058Z-1723229578-RC2IPLAHRTG4-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-UGANDA.jpg">© Abubaker Lubowa / REUTERS</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal's Faye pays first visit to Mali since appointment as Ecowas president</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260728-senegal-s-diomaye-faye-on-a-visit-to-mali-his-first-as-ecowas-president</link><description>
Senegalese President Bassirou Diomaye Faye was in Bamako on Tuesday for a one-day working visit – in a dual capacity, as both head of state of Senegal and current chair of Ecowas. He is scheduled to hold talks with his Malian counterpart, Assimi Goïta, just days after launching his own political party in Dakar.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/429f778e-21ce-11ef-8af9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-05-30T204719Z_1066833909_RC2518ALCMU6_RTRMADP_3_WESTAFRICA-POLITICS.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/429f778e-21ce-11ef-8af9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-05-30T204719Z_1066833909_RC2518ALCMU6_RTRMADP_3_WESTAFRICA-POLITICS.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">193c8234-8a71-11f1-aaeb-0331a7041faa</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:42:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/429f778e-21ce-11ef-8af9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2024-05-30T204719Z_1066833909_RC2518ALCMU6_RTRMADP_3_WESTAFRICA-POLITICS.JPG">via REUTERS - Senegalese Presidency</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal's Faye breaks ties with Sonko to launch new political party</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260728-diomaye-faye-breaks-with-sonko-launches-new-party-in-senegal</link><description>
Senegal's President Bassirou Diomaye Faye on Saturday launched a new political party called Kiiraay, following his high-profile falling-out with his former mentor and ex-prime minister, Ousmane Sonko, and his party Pastef.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a329ea56-8998-11f1-9b75-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Senegal-Kiiraay-launch-Diomaye-Faye-July2026-afp-000-C37Q6F7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a329ea56-8998-11f1-9b75-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Senegal-Kiiraay-launch-Diomaye-Faye-July2026-afp-000-C37Q6F7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">76d84dd0-8998-11f1-ba77-9f6e96b6eca3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 08:30:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a329ea56-8998-11f1-9b75-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Senegal-Kiiraay-launch-Diomaye-Faye-July2026-afp-000-C37Q6F7.jpg">AFP - SEYLLOU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Niger’s junta marks three years amid rising violence and lost freedoms</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260727-niger-s-junta-marks-three-years-amid-rising-violence-and-lost-freedoms</link><description>
Three years after President Mohamed Bazoum was overthrown, Niger is recording strong oil-driven growth but facing rising jihadist violence and a severe restriction of political freedoms, former ambassador Kiari Liman-Tinguiri tells RFI.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef733f3a-6f89-11f1-bcbb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-02T174426Z-1858663520-RC2TLLA1NAF5-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-NIGER-DIPLOMACY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef733f3a-6f89-11f1-bcbb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-02T174426Z-1858663520-RC2TLLA1NAF5-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-NIGER-DIPLOMACY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb55aeee-89b3-11f1-9a3f-459da0914a80</guid><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:02:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef733f3a-6f89-11f1-bcbb-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-02T174426Z-1858663520-RC2TLLA1NAF5-RTRMADP-3-BENIN-NIGER-DIPLOMACY.jpg">via REUTERS - Niger Presidency</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ebola surges past 3,200 cases in DRC as Oxford begins first vaccine trial</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260727-ebola-surges-past-3-200-cases-in-drc-as-oxford-begins-first-vaccine-trial</link><description>
The death toll from an Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has climbed to 1,405, with confirmed cases now at 3,200, government data showed Sunday, as researchers race to develop a vaccine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3aaa4664-8994-11f1-8e9f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EBOLA-DRC-minister-visit-2026-07-25-rtrs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3aaa4664-8994-11f1-8e9f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EBOLA-DRC-minister-visit-2026-07-25-rtrs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b51cc89c-8992-11f1-9124-07d1b4f8dfb8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 10:29:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3aaa4664-8994-11f1-8e9f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EBOLA-DRC-minister-visit-2026-07-25-rtrs.jpg">REUTERS - Gradel Muyisa Mumbere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ecowas greenlights $25bn Nigeria-Morocco mega gas pipeline</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-ecowas-greenlights-25bn-mega-gas-pipeline-nigeria-morocco</link><description>
West African leaders have approved plans for a gas pipeline linking Nigeria to Morocco, marking a major political milestone for one of Africa's most ambitious infrastructure projects.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">596d58c6-851f-11f1-8b17-3366361549e6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 08:54:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5fc30d46-85d9-11f1-b888-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par8293056.jpg">AFP - FLORIAN PLAUCHEUR</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird with RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal ready to show ‘what it is capable of’ at Dakar 2026 Youth Olympics</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260726-senegal-ready-to-show-what-it-is-capable-of-at-dakar-2026-youth-olympics</link><description>
With venues nearing completion and public enthusiasm growing, Dakar 2026 chief organiser Ibrahima Wade tells RFI that Senegal is ready to make Olympic history when the Youth Games begin on 31 October.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c11d46d6-866c-11f1-8b0d-07709273a6e7</guid><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 05:14:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e138c88-8655-11f1-9023-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-93F67HH-1.jpg">AFP - SEYLLOU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>More health workers strike as Ebola cases in Congo near 3,000, including over 1,300 deaths</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260725-more-health-workers-strike-as-ebola-cases-in-congo-near-3-000-including-over-1-300-deaths</link><description>
Health workers at an Ebola treatment center in eastern Congo went on strike Saturday over payment issues, disrupting care for patients in the epicenter of the country’s rapidly growing outbreak.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a0aa694-8833-11f1-a8ad-1172a0685593</guid><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:21:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg">AP Photo/Dirole Lotsima Dieudonn - Dirole Lotsima Dieudonne</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Heatwave hits North Africa, with power cuts in Tunisia and wildfires in Algeria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260724-heatwave-hits-north-africa-with-power-cuts-in-tunisia-and-wildfires-in-algeria</link><description>
In Tunisia long power outages across the country have added to the strain of an intense heatwave, with temperatures as high as 49C. In neighbouring Algeria, more than 100 people were hospitalised after wildfires, the country's interior minister said this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84103238-8736-11f1-a751-f3778ee5cdf9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 21:04:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/98e62ef2-873a-11f1-9b15-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/algeria-fire-july2026-afp-000-C2QK7EK.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ghanaians ask ICC to investigate xenophobic violence in South Africa</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260724-ghanaians-ask-icc-to-investigate-xenophobic-violence-in-south-africa</link><description>
Two Ghanaian nationals have petitioned the International Criminal Court to open a preliminary investigation into attacks on foreign nationals in South Africa, arguing the violence could amount to crimes against humanity, as Ghana's president repeated his call on Thursday for the African Union to address the ongoing unrest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9a45fb74-866d-11f1-b5d0-5ba20fd9084b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:58:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/2c307f66-7c12-11f1-9589-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-09T111435Z-177337990-RC29AMAPR5F1-RTRMADP-3-SAFRICA-XENOPHOBIA.jpg">© REUTERS - Oupa Nkosi </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC's Ebola outbreak kills more than 1,000, with children hit hardest</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260723-drc-s-ebola-outbreak-kills-more-than-1-000-with-children-hit-hardest</link><description>
More than 1,030 people have died from an Ebola outbreak declared in May in the Democratic Republic of Congo and Uganda, the World Health Organization said on Wednesday, as confirmed cases in the DRC surpassed 2,530, according to government data.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">75b61aee-866f-11f1-893a-5ba20fd9084b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 09:51:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2ff3fe8-866f-11f1-85f8-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26203634145364.jpg">AP Photo/Dirole Lotsima Dieudonn - Dirole Lotsima Dieudonne</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>DRC opposition postpones protest after Tshisekedi announces national dialogue</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260722-drc-opposition-postpones-protest-after-tshisekedi-announces-national-dialogue</link><description>
The Democratic Republic of Congo's main opposition coalition has postponed a protest after President Félix Tshisekedi announced the imminent launch of a national dialogue, a bid to ease the country's deepening political stand-off.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/896fce52-f07b-11f0-9e48-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87682AK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/896fce52-f07b-11f0-9e48-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87682AK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">632cc468-85a2-11f1-bacc-97e9dac3ef9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 15:49:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/896fce52-f07b-11f0-9e48-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87682AK.jpg">© AFP - ANDREW CABALLERO-REYNOLDS </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Gabon and France deepen industrial cooperation with Eramet manganese deal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260722-gabon-and-france-deepen-industrial-cooperation-with-eramet-manganese-deal</link><description>
French mining group Eramet is considering a major expansion of manganese processing in Gabon under an agreement that could strengthen the country’s industrial base, modernise its railway network and reduce its reliance on exports of unprocessed ore.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f66a1f82-84f8-11f1-b95b-159cb199153e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:52:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a5bbb926-8488-11f1-9289-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26201639434838.jpg">© Ludovic Marin / Pool AFP via AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Senegal's Faye backs former president Sall's bid for UN top job in U-turn</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260721-senegal-s-faye-backs-ex-president-sall-s-bid-for-un-top-job-in-u-turn</link><description>
Senegalese President Bassirou Diomaye Faye has endorsed former president Macky Sall's candidacy to become the next United Nations secretary-general, the foreign ministry said on Monday, giving his predecessor crucial backing from his home country despite deep political divisions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">86f1bada-84d9-11f1-8d9c-db2ffabab7f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:37:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0c655eb0-84c1-11f1-a1d4-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-34MQ7N7.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight on Africa</category><title>Countdown to the ballot: Zambia gears up for August elections</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/spotlight-on-africa/20260721-countdown-to-the-ballot-zambia-gears-up-for-august-elections</link><description>
This week on Spotlight on Africa, we're heading to Zambia, where general elections are set to take place on the 13th August. Voters will go to the polls to elect a president, members of the National Assembly, councillors and council chairs. Incumbent President Hakainde Hichilema has already picked up endorsements from within his own camp, the UPND Alliance, the coalition that's held power since 2021. So what's at stake, and who's in the running?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df361890-5675-11f1-b9ec-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Le-pr%C3%A9sident-zambien-Hakainde-Hichilema-%C3%A0-Harare-au-Zimbabwe-le-14-novembre-2025.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/df361890-5675-11f1-b9ec-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Le-pr%C3%A9sident-zambien-Hakainde-Hichilema-%C3%A0-Harare-au-Zimbabwe-le-14-novembre-2025.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">566666c0-7eaf-11f1-8b4b-d7a352c90397</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:41:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Melissa Chemam</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>US slaps new sanctions on Sudan after chlorine gas deployment claims</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260720-us-slaps-new-sanctions-on-sudan-after-chlorine-gas-deployment-claims</link><description>
The United States has imposed new airspace bans and financing restrictions on Sudan's military-led government, accusing it of using chemical weapons in its war against rival RSF paramilitaries. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c290a986-37cb-11f0-936d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_43VR9T2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c290a986-37cb-11f0-936d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_43VR9T2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc4353a2-842a-11f1-892a-9faf196e7847</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:58:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c290a986-37cb-11f0-936d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_43VR9T2.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>France welcomes Gabon's Oligui as mineral and military ties defy African rift</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260720-france-welcomes-gabon-s-oligui-as-mineral-and-military-ties-defy-wider-rift-in-africa</link><description>
